FFmpeg: the OpenH264 wrapper's functions named outside zebkit's exports.

patches/1090 renames OpenH264's WelsCreateSVCEncoder() and
WelsDestroySVCEncoder() to the C wrapper's (//zebkit/ffmpeg/openh264_c_api.cc),
which are hidden, as the rest of the engine but its API. Named zebkit_*, they
matched macOS's -exported_symbol _zebkit_*, and ld64.lld refuses to export a
hidden symbol: the macOS engine did not link. openh264_zebkit_*, outside the
pattern, on every system.

diff --git a/third_party/ffmpeg/libavcodec/libopenh264enc.c b/third_party/ffmpeg/libavcodec/libopenh264enc.c
--- a/third_party/ffmpeg/libavcodec/libopenh264enc.c
+++ b/third_party/ffmpeg/libavcodec/libopenh264enc.c
@@ -22,8 +22,8 @@
 /* zebkit: the encoder through an object of OpenH264's C layout
  * (//zebkit/ffmpeg/openh264_c_api.cc), which C can call under any C++ vtable
  * ABI; zebkit's Linux build has Clang's relative vtables. */
-#define WelsCreateSVCEncoder zebkit_openh264_create_encoder
-#define WelsDestroySVCEncoder zebkit_openh264_destroy_encoder
+#define WelsCreateSVCEncoder openh264_zebkit_create_encoder
+#define WelsDestroySVCEncoder openh264_zebkit_destroy_encoder
 #include <wels/codec_api.h>
 #include <wels/codec_ver.h>
 
